"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith=self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith||[]).push([[15924],{715924:n=>{n.exports='# Logging & Registration\n\nLog models to MLflow and register to Unity Catalog. This covers classical ML, custom PyFunc, and HuggingFace transformer models.\n\n> **MLflow API note:** Examples below use `name=`, the current MLflow 3.x keyword. On runtimes with MLflow 2.x, substitute `artifact_path=` instead — it\'s deprecated on 3.x but still functional, and it\'s the only form recognized on 2.x.\n\n## Critical: Always Include signature AND input_example\n\nWhen logging models to Unity Catalog, **always** include both `signature` and `input_example`. These are required for Model Serving to validate inputs, generate API documentation, and enable the serving UI.\n\n## Classical ML (Autolog)\n\nThe simplest approach — train and everything is logged automatically:\n\n```python\nimport mlflow\n\nmlflow.sklearn.autolog(\n    log_input_examples=True,\n    registered_model_name="main.models.my_classifier"\n)\n\nmodel = LogisticRegression()\nmodel.fit(X_train, y_train)\n```\n\nSupported autolog frameworks: `mlflow.sklearn`, `mlflow.xgboost`, `mlflow.lightgbm`, `mlflow.pytorch`, `mlflow.tensorflow`, `mlflow.spark`.\n\n## Classical ML (Manual Logging)\n\nWhen autolog isn\'t sufficient (custom metrics, multiple models, etc.):\n\n```python\nimport mlflow\nfrom mlflow.models import infer_signature\n\nmlflow.set_registry_uri("databricks-uc")\n\nwith mlflow.start_run():\n    model = RandomForestClassifier(n_estimators=100)\n    model.fit(X_train, y_train)\n\n    accuracy = model.score(X_test, y_test)\n    mlflow.log_metric("accuracy", accuracy)\n\n    signature = infer_signature(X_train, model.predict(X_train))\n\n    model_info = mlflow.sklearn.log_model(\n        model,\n        name="model",\n        signature=signature,\n        input_example=X_train[:5],\n        registered_model_name="main.models.random_forest",\n    )\n```\n\n## HuggingFace Transformers\n\nWhen logging HuggingFace models, **always wrap them in a pipeline** before logging. Do not pass raw model objects (e.g., `AutoModelForSequenceClassification`) directly to `mlflow.transformers.log_model`.\n\n```python\nimport mlflow\nfrom transformers import pipeline\n\nclassifier = pipeline(\n    "text-classification",\n    model="distilbert-base-uncased-finetuned-sst-2-english",\n)\n\nsignature = mlflow.models.infer_signature(\n    model_input="This is a test",\n    model_output=classifier("This is a test"),\n)\n\nwith mlflow.start_run():\n    model_info = mlflow.transformers.log_model(\n        transformers_model=classifier,\n        name="model",\n        signature=signature,\n        input_example=["This is a test sentence"],\n        registered_model_name="main.models.text_classifier",\n    )\n```\n\n## Custom PyFunc Models\n\nFor models with custom preprocessing, postprocessing, or complex inference logic:\n\n```python\nimport mlflow\nimport pandas as pd\n\nclass MyCustomModel(mlflow.pyfunc.PythonModel):\n    def load_context(self, context):\n        import pickle\n        with open(context.artifacts["preprocessor"], "rb") as f:\n            self.preprocessor = pickle.load(f)\n        with open(context.artifacts["model"], "rb") as f:\n            self.model = pickle.load(f)\n\n    def predict(self, context, model_input: pd.DataFrame) -> pd.DataFrame:\n        processed = self.preprocessor.transform(model_input)\n        predictions = self.model.predict(processed)\n        return pd.DataFrame({"prediction": predictions})\n\n\nwith mlflow.start_run():\n    mlflow.pyfunc.log_model(\n        name="model",\n        python_model=MyCustomModel(),\n        artifacts={\n            "preprocessor": "artifacts/preprocessor.pkl",\n            "model": "artifacts/model.pkl",\n        },\n        signature=signature,\n        input_example={"age": 25, "income": 50000, "category": "A"},\n        pip_requirements=["scikit-learn==1.3.0", "pandas"],\n        registered_model_name="main.models.custom_model",\n    )\n```\n\n## Defining Signatures\n\n```python\nfrom mlflow.models import infer_signature, ModelSignature\nfrom mlflow.types.schema import Schema, ColSpec\n\n# Option 1: Infer from data (preferred)\nsignature = infer_signature(\n    model_input=X_sample,\n    model_output=predictions_sample,\n)\n\n# Option 2: Define explicitly\ninput_schema = Schema([\n    ColSpec("double", "age"),\n    ColSpec("double", "income"),\n    ColSpec("string", "category"),\n])\noutput_schema = Schema([\n    ColSpec("double", "probability"),\n    ColSpec("string", "class"),\n])\nsignature = ModelSignature(inputs=input_schema, outputs=output_schema)\n```\n\n## GenAI Agent Logging (File-Based)\n\nFor LangGraph or ResponsesAgent agents, log from a Python file:\n\n```python\nimport mlflow\nfrom mlflow.models.resources import DatabricksServingEndpoint\n\nmlflow.set_registry_uri("databricks-uc")\n\nresources = [DatabricksServingEndpoint(endpoint_name="databricks-meta-llama-3-3-70b-instruct")]\n\ninput_example = {\n    "input": [{"role": "user", "content": "What is Databricks?"}]\n}\n\nwith mlflow.start_run():\n    model_info = mlflow.pyfunc.log_model(\n        name="agent",\n        python_model="agent.py",\n        input_example=input_example,\n        resources=resources,\n        pip_requirements=[\n            "mlflow==3.6.0",\n            "databricks-langchain",\n            "langgraph==0.3.4",\n        ],\n    )\n\nmlflow.register_model(\n    model_uri=model_info.model_uri,\n    name="main.agents.my_agent",\n)\n```\n\n## Pre-Deployment Validation\n\nAlways validate the model loads and runs before deploying:\n\n```python\nmlflow.models.predict(\n    model_uri=model_info.model_uri,\n    input_data={"age": 25, "income": 50000},\n    env_manager="uv",\n)\n```\n\n## Common Issues\n\n| Issue                             | Solution                                           |\n| --------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| Package not found at serving time | Specify exact versions in `pip_requirements`       |\n| Auth error accessing endpoint     | Add resource to `resources` list when logging      |\n| Model signature mismatch          | Provide `input_example` matching your input format |\n| Slow model loading                | Use `env_manager="uv"` for faster validation       |\n'}}]);
